      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "@{58c6d558ff44e44ada717902|full_name}: I think it'd be preferable for immersion/group use for the screenshot/snapshot to be via a spawnable in-game object with both a front (for \"selfies\") and rear (for traditional use) viewfinder. You could cut down on rendering costs by making the model simple, and only rendering the front/rear viewfinder for the user that spawned that particular camera. Additionally you could mark the camera for the user such that it would be easy for a user to identify \"their\" camera in a pile of spawned user cameras.\n\nHowever, having this PLUS a quick in-menu \"snapshot current user view\" button would be nice. Maybe even a shortcut (trigger + menu button?) for quick captures.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
